[b]Automates your party's logistics. Ride into a town and your steward works out what you need — food, horses, troops, prisoners, loot — and does it all with one click (or by itself, if you let it).[/b]

One table shows what the steward will do. Nudge any row, then press [b]Deal all[/b].

[size=5][b]What your steward does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Food[/b]: keeps enough for everyone (40 days by default, at your party's own rate), buys the kinds you have least of first for variety and morale, sells real surplus.
[*][b]Horses[/b]: keeps your pack animals (10 by default) and a horse for every footman, with the war horses you choose to keep. Cheapest bought, surplus sold dearest first; lame ones replaced.
[*][b]Troops[/b]: the recruits the notables offer you, then your own troops: recruit or dismiss with a click.
[*][b]Tavern[/b]: wanderers and mercenaries for hire, each with a click. Never suggested: you choose.
[*][b]Prisoners[/b]: ransomed in towns, or donated for influence to your kingdom's dungeons, in towns and castles.
[*][b]Loot[/b]: armour and weapons sold in groups, cheapest first or most kilos per denar. Pieces you lock in the inventory are never sold.
[*][b]Your goals and quests[/b]: type your own number for any food or horse row; what your quests ask for is never sold.
[*][b]Full-autonomous steward[/b] (off by default): on arrival it does it all without the window, never lets your gold drop below 100,000, and leaves a short report in the message log.
[/list]
Money has an order: sell first, then food, then horses, with gold floors you set. By default nothing is bought above the average price +20% or sold below −20%.

[size=5][b]How to use it[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Enter a town or village: the [b]Party Steward[/b] opens by itself when there is something to do. Or pick it from the town, village or castle menu.
[*][b][–] [+][/b] on any row: click ±1, Shift ±5, Ctrl all. Every line has its own [b]Deal[/b], every group a [b]Deal group[/b].
[*]Everything goes through the game's own trade, ransom and hiring, so Trade XP and quests count as if you did it by hand.
[*][b]Prices[/b] tab: your own price book. [b]Instructions[/b] tab: every standing order.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]None. No Harmony.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/612]Mod Configuration Menu (MCM)[/url] is optional. Every setting is also in the window and in a commented [i]settings.json[/i].
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] click Mod Manager Download and enable it.
[*][b]Manual:[/b] extract the zip into [i]Mount & Blade II Bannerlord\Modules\[/i], so you get [i]Modules\SmartSteward\SubModule.xml[/i]. Enable it in the launcher (below MCM if you use it).
[/list]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Game v1.4.8, singleplayer. Works with or without War Sails.
[*]Nothing is stored in your save: safe to add or remove mid-campaign.
[*]Castles have no market, so there the steward only donates prisoners. Trade goods are not handled yet. English only for now; translations welcome ([i]ModuleData\Languages\std_SmartSteward.xml[/i]).
[*]Settings file and log: [i]Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\SmartSteward\[/i]. Attach [i]smart_steward.log[/i] to a bug report.
[*]Also on the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3817263044]Steam Workshop[/url] and on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/smart_steward/releases/latest]GitHub Releases[/url]. Same files.
[/list]

Bugs or a mod it fights with: tell me in the comments or on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/smart_steward/issues]GitHub[/url]. The full design: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/smart_steward/blob/main/docs/DESIGN.md]docs/DESIGN.md[/url].

Made by two of us: the code and all technical work by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea, feedback and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

